en facebook is  not safe from being replaced  historically the social media space has  always been a fast moving world as  people jumped from one platform to the  next first there was friendster and then  we saw the rise of myspace followed up  by the explosions of twitter and  facebook after this initial web-based  era we saw a new era centered around  apps including whatsapp and instagram  and then snapchat and now tick tock  considering this rapid evolution  investors have always been wary of  investing in social media companies the  next big thing could become yesterday's  news within just a few years  for example y'all remember vine yik yak  or google plus  clearly things change on a dime within  the social media industry despite this  with facebook many investors felt that  things would be different as industries  mature they can support bigger and more  stable companies for instance just take  a look at google when they launched in  the late 1990s there were dozens of  different search engines on the market  and they each had a sizable user base  but over time one search engine after  another fell off the map and the google  rose as the winner  the same thing could be said about the  browser and email spaces as well  initially the crown was passed around  frequently but with the time there was  only one winner considering this many  investors felt that facebook would  become the google of social media and  facebook has actually done a tremendous  job at accomplishing this we just have  to take one look at facebook stock  versus twitter stock to understand just  how well facebook has done it even with  the recent decline despite this strong  performance over the years it has become  clear that facebook is not really  comparable to google you see with google  while they have completed dozens of  insane acquisitions over the years each  of these have expanded the business not  cannibalized the old business google's  original services including google.com  gmail 